GT-MHA residual ablation:

Keep the standard MHA command unchanged for the baseline. For the matched
GT-MHA run, add only:

 --attention_type gt_mha_residual \
 --gt_mha_num_base_heads 4 \
 --gt_mha_num_generators 8 \

The default attention type remains `mha`. When loading a standard MHA
checkpoint into GT-MHA, the loader averages adjacent pretrained Q/K/V heads
into the four shared bases and copies the output projection. Generator
parameters use the native GT-MHA initialization.

